.\" ABSD manual page source (mdoc(7)); rendered by scripts/render-man.sh.
.Dd October 12, 2026
.Dt TEST 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm test
.Nd evaluate an expression (sbase)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar expression
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is sbase 0.1's
.Nm test ,
built for ABSD with the C kit and two declared patches
.Pq Pa userland/patches/test-access-mtime.patch , test-stdout-gate.patch ;
see
.Xr sbase 7 .
It evaluates a file, string or integer expression and reports the result
in its exit status only; it prints nothing on success.
The file tests
.Fl e , Fl f , Fl d , Fl r , Fl s ,
and the string and integer comparisons, behave as upstream.
The read, write and execute tests use
.Fn access
where upstream uses
.Fn faccessat ,
which ABSD does not provide; with one fixed identity the two answer alike.
.Sh UNSUPPORTED ON ABSD
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl w Ar DIR
status 2,
.Ql test: -w DIR: check not supported on this system: Function not implemented
(SPEC A11).
.It Fl x Ar FILE
status 2,
.Ql ... check not supported on this system: Invalid argument
(no execute permission exists);
.Fl x Ar DIR
is true.
.It Fl nt , Fl ot
status 2,
.Ql test: -nt/-ot: file modification times are not available on this system .
.It Fl h , Fl L , Fl p , Fl S , Fl b , Fl c
false: only files and directories exist (A13).
.It Fl u , Fl g , Fl k
false: modes are 0644/0444 only.
.It Fl t Ar FD
false: no descriptor is a terminal
.Pf ( Fn isatty
0).
.It Li \&[ No form
the binary honours
.Ql argv[0]
.Ql \&[ ,
but no
.Pa /bin/[
is installed.
.El
.Pp
Behaviour on ABSD is predicted until the guest qualification
.Pq Xr sbase 7 .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when the expression is true, 1 when it is false, 2 on an error or one of
the refusals above.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
absd$ test -d /home/operator && echo yes
yes
absd$ test -f /etc/missing
absd-sh: test: exit status 1
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr absd-sh 1 ,
